I'm just I'm trying to figure out the  logic of all of this the timing of all  of this why on a Saturday and that's why  we're bringing in Mike Florio from pro  football talk and NBC football night in  America Mike good morning thanks for  joining us why now  that's a great question Dan because look  some people think it's a PR move by the  NFL to do this well why would you do it  now everything's done everything's over  Kaepernick's agent put out a memo a few  weeks ago addressing some of the false  narratives it's still linger about Colin  Kaepernick it didn't even register a  blip on the radar screen people don't  care people have moved on I don't know  why the league would decide right now we  got to have this workout on a Saturday  in November where all teams are going to  be invited no one's gonna be there I  mean they'll send low-level lackeys to  cover this thing and maybe a coach in a  GM oh look at the film of it but a  workouts not meaningful unless the coach  is there the GM is there they're not  going to be there and that's why  Kaepernick's agents said initially the  league can we do it on Tuesday the  league said no well can we do it next  Saturday so teams have more time to do  this league says no so there's a weird  vibe to this there's something else  going on more than meets the eye  any team out there can bring him in for  a workout anytime they want the idea of  the league office has decided out of the  blue we're gonna have this workout where  all 32 teams are invited and it's going  to be this Saturday and only this  Saturday there's just something about it  that doesn't smell right and if it's PR  it's clumsy PR Dan I think at a certain  level they're worried about a second  lawsuit from Colin Kaepernick for  retaliating against him because of the  first one you know he follows the first  one they pay him and then they continue  to freeze him out the argument now would  be the reason no one's giving him a job  is they're upset they had to write him a  big check and as we see these fringe  level quarterbacks who are thriving why  does that this guy even get a workout he  doesn't even get a phone call and this  is the NFL's possibly possibly clumsy  way of enhancing their legal standing if  there is a second lawsuit somewhere down  the road from Kaepernick what's more  important on Saturday the actual workout  with Kaepernick or the interview with  Kaepernick I think the workouts more  important Dan because look these teams  have been in position to find out  everything they want to find out how  much money does he want what's he  expecting that  have treated him like he doesn't exist  they don't want to know the answers to  the questions they've allowed the false  narratives to take root and there are  people who say well he wants 20 million  a year well he only wants to be a  starter well he's a vegan  well he's this yeah and and these are  easy questions to get answers to if they  want them but it's been crickets for two  and a half years and really the best  argument that the teams have now to stay  away from him is the fact that he hasn't  played since January 1 of 2017 and the  reason he hasn't played since then is  because they successfully frozen him out  so that's what's so strange about this  they're at a point where everyone's  moved on and everyone's accepted I've  been a cavernous reporter from day one  and I've accepted he's not getting back  in it is so bizarre to me that all of a  sudden they would do this but yeah we'll  see and who's gonna be there to  interview him that's the thing if a  coach at a GM isn't there and they send  some low-level scout how meaningful is  that interview going to be so the just  the whole thing stinks to me and and you  know I I'd love to know how this came to  be I'd love to know who's bright idea  this was I'd love to know how many  owners actually knew about this before  this is something the league office  decided to do I had a source who told me  this morning because I said where's this  coming from and its source said there's  pressure on the commissioner and I said  who's applying the pressure and he said  I can't talk about it now what the hell  is going on here I mean it's a jzi Sims  and I were talking about this earlier  damn PFT live and Sims throughout the  jay-z angle and my thought is if jay-z  was in any way responsible for this that  would have been leaked because he's  gonna want credit for us to push back  against all the criticism he got so if  no one's linking jay-z to this it's not  jay-z so I don't know where the pressure  would be on the commissioner unless the  pressure is coming from his in-house  lawyer Jeff pash saying we need to do  something here we needed weight no one's  giving this guy a workout we need to we  need to have a workout for him and maybe  he won't show up but if he doesn't show  up and we can say he's really not  serious about playing football and it  may be that it's just his weird game of  chess that they're they're gonna throw  the enforcers they're gonna throw these  bread crumbs out there and see if he  follows the trail and if he doesn't then  they put themselves in a better spot if  there would be further litigation down  the road but this one is one of the more  bizarre developments it's you know it's  unforced error from the league at a time  when they want everyone to focus on the  100 season they're the ones who have  dusted this off and put this front and  center and there was no reason to do it  if I gave you one question privately for  Colin Kaepernick what would you ask him  I'd want to know will he accept coming  in and taking a veteran minimum salary  and being a member of the depth chart  there to compete and prepare and and  just and you know and and just work and  just go to work and not expect anything  other than a spot on the team with an  opportunity to show in practice what he  can do and because really what can you  do on the fly you're trying to change  the tire on a moving car if you come in  playing quarterback the only place where  it would make sense is Baltimore where  Greg Roman is the offensive coordinator  let me tell you if Lamar Jackson gets  injured they better call Colin  Kaepernick because then it's down to RG  three and if they want to finish out  this special season they have going and  Jackson does get injured Kaepernick is  the only thing that's going to keep this  on track for the Baltimore Ravens great  stuff Mike thank you we appreciate your  time as always i dancey buddy that's  Mike Florio Pro Football Talk live  co-host and NBC football night in  America for more Dan Patrick show tune  in the audience Channel 239 on DirecTV  stream for free on BR live or download  the Dan Patrick show app  [Music]

